.\" conflux(1): the daemon and its CLI. The config file is in conflux(5).
.\" Keep in step with the CLI (crates/conflux/src/main.rs); a test checks that
.\" every command and option is named here.
.TH CONFLUX 1 "" "conflux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
conflux \- background file-sync daemon and its control commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY conflux
.RB [ \-\-system ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR name ]
.B daemon
.YS
.SY conflux
.RI [ options ]
.B status
.YS
.SY conflux
.RI [ options ]
.B sync
.RB [ \-n ]
.RI [ group ]
.YS
.SY conflux
.RI [ options ]
.B reload
.YS
.SY conflux
.RI [ options ]
.B config
.BR validate | show | paths
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B conflux
keeps local directories in step with a WebDAV server, a git repository or
another directory, or keeps a git clone up to date through git itself.
What to sync and when is written in a TOML file, described in
.BR conflux (5).
.PP
One binary is both the daemon and the commands that control it.
.B conflux daemon
runs the syncs of one profile in the foreground; it is usually started by its
systemd unit (see
.BR UNITS ).
The other commands talk to a running daemon over its control socket, except
.BR config ,
which reads the file itself.
.PP
Each sync group runs on its trigger: on local changes, on a timer, or only when
asked, and optionally also polls the remote for changes.
Deletions are not propagated unless a group allows them, files above a size
limit are skipped, and when a file changed on both sides the newer one is kept
in place and the other as a conflict copy next to it (see
.BR conflux (5)).
.SS Scopes
A daemon runs in one of two scopes:
.TP
.B user
The default for a user other than root.
The config, the state and the socket are under
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME
and
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
(see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.B system
With
.BR \-\-system ,
or always when run as root.
The config, the state and the socket are under
.IR /etc ,
.I /var/lib
and
.IR /run .
The system daemon runs as the
.B conflux
user.
.SS Profiles
A profile selects which daemon a command targets, and which sync groups that
daemon runs: those whose
.B profiles
list names it, and for the
.B default
profile also those without a
.B profiles
list.
So one shared config file can drive different hosts, or several daemons on one
host, each with its own state directory and control socket.
Profile names are 1 to 64 ASCII letters, digits,
.BR _ ,
.B \-
and
.BR . ,
not starting with
.B .\&
or
.BR \- .
.SH OPTIONS
These options can be given before or after the command.
.TP
.B \-\-system
Use the system scope: its config file, state directory and socket.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIpath\fR"
Read this config file instead of the scope's.
Overrides
.BR CONFLUX_CONFIG .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile " \fIname\fR"
Target the daemon of this profile, or for
.BR daemon ,
run it.
Defaults to
.BR default ,
or for
.B daemon
to the config's
.B [daemon] profile
setting.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help, for
.B conflux
or for the command it follows.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the daemon in the foreground, logging to standard error, until it gets
.B SIGTERM
or
.BR SIGINT .
It syncs every group of its profile once at startup, whatever the group's
trigger, then runs each one on its trigger.
A config with errors is refused: the daemon does not start.
.TP
.B status
Show each sync group of the daemon: its label, trigger and local root, and its
last run with a summary or the error.
.TP
.BR sync " [" \-n "] [\fIgroup\fR]"
Sync now and wait for the result.
.I group
is a sync's
.B id
or its label, as
.B status
shows it:
.IB remote : remote_path\fR,
the remote alone without a
.BR remote_path ,
or for a
.B git_repo
group the name of its directory.
Without it, every group of the profile syncs.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what the sync would change, changing nothing.
The daemon fetches the remote's state to compare against but writes, deletes
and pushes nothing.
Each line is a path with what would happen to it:
.B \[u2191]
upload,
.B \[u2193]
download,
.B \[u2717]
delete,
.B !
conflict (with the copy that would win),
.B \[u00B7]
skip.
Conflicts are predicted from modification times, so a file that turns out to be
identical on both sides may show as one.
.IP
A dry run previews the next sync of a running daemon, that is the changes made
since its last one; it cannot preview a group the daemon has not run yet, as it
syncs every group at startup.
.RE
.TP
.B reload
Have the daemon read its config file again, without restarting.
A config with errors is refused, and the daemon keeps the one it has.
.TP
.B config validate
Check the config file as the daemon would, then print warnings for settings
that are accepted but probably not what was meant.
.TP
.B config show
Print the config as the daemon reads it, with every default filled in.
.TP
.B config paths
Print the config file, state directory and control socket that the scope and
profile resolve to.
.SH PERMISSIONS
A user daemon's socket is in the user's own runtime directory.
A system daemon's socket is open to every local user, who can read its
.BR status ,
as the config it describes is readable by everyone.
.BR sync ,
.B sync \-n
and
.B reload
of a system daemon need root, the
.B conflux
user, or membership in the
.B conflux
group.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the config, as
.B conflux reload
does.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Stop the daemon.
.SH UNITS
The packages install systemd units for both scopes:
.B conflux.service
runs the
.B default
profile and
.BI conflux@ profile .service
any other.
User daemons are managed with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user" ,
system daemons with
.BR systemctl ;
.B journalctl
shows their logs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The daemon passes its environment on to the commands it runs, such as
.B password_command
and
.BR commit_msg_command .
.TP
.B CONFLUX_CONFIG
The config file, in place of the scope's.
.TP
.B CONFLUX_LOG
What to log: a level
.RB ( error ,
.BR warn ,
.BR info ,
.BR debug ,
.BR trace )
or a tracing filter such as
.BR info,conflux_core=debug .
Overrides the config's
.BR log_level .
Defaults to
.BR info .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The user config's directory, by default
.IR \(ti/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
The user state's directory, by default
.IR \(ti/.local/state .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Holds the user daemons' sockets in its
.I conflux
directory; without it they are in the state directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \(ti/.config/conflux/config.toml
The user config.
.TP
.I /etc/conflux/config.toml
The system config.
.TP
.IR \(ti/.local/state/conflux/ ", " /var/lib/conflux/
State: the index of each sync group, and the clones of
.B git
remotes.
A profile other than
.B default
has a directory of the profile's name in it.
.TP
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/conflux/conflux.sock ", " /run/conflux/conflux.sock
The control socket of the
.B default
profile's daemon;
.BI conflux\- profile .sock
for any other.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
when the command or any sync group it ran failed,
.B 2
for invalid usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the user daemon, now and at every login:
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now conflux
.EE
.RE
.PP
See what a sync of the group
.B dotfiles
would change, then run it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
conflux sync \-n dotfiles
conflux sync dotfiles
.EE
.RE
.PP
Show the status of the system daemon of the profile
.BR backup :
.PP
.RS
.EX
conflux \-\-system \-p backup status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Try a config in the foreground, with debug logs, before installing it:
.PP
.RS
.EX
CONFLUX_LOG=debug conflux \-c /tmp/try.toml daemon
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR conflux (5),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR git (1)
.PP
The project, with more documentation and Conflux, a GNOME app for the same
config and daemons:
.br
.UR https://github.com/AperteDev/conflux
.UE
